      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "ExtUtils::Typemaps::STL::List versions before 1.07 for Perl allocate a 32 GiB array on an empty list.\n\nThe OUTPUT typemaps call av_extend( av, len-1 ). On an empty list, this undeflows, and av_extend will allocate an array with 2^32 slots, leading to memory exhaustion.\n\nNote that a similar issue was fixed in ExtUtils::Typemaps::STL::Vector version 1.05.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
